  "reasoning": "Step 1: Trouble breathing during exercise suggests cardiovascular strain or general fatigue/weakness, which are common complications of uncontrolled blood sugar levels.\nStep 2: Sweating excessively and getting hot easily points to autonomic nervous system dysfunction or metabolic dysregulation, frequently observed in diabetic patients.\nStep 3: Recurrent yeast infections are a classic and highly specific indicator of diabetes, as elevated glucose levels in bodily fluids create an ideal environment for fungal (yeast) overgrowth.\nSynthesizing these symptoms, the combination of exertional breathlessness, thermoregulatory abnormalities, and recurrent fungal infections strongly indicates diabetes.",
